#. radio type
#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:297
msgid "Radio type"
msgstr "Radiotype"

#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:310
msgid "FT817/857/897 (manual)"
msgstr "FT817/857/897 (manuel)"

#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:314
msgid ""
"<b>RX only:</b>  The radio shall only be used as receiver. If <i>Monitor PTT "
"status</i> is checked the doppler tuning will be suspended while PTT is ON "
"(manual TX). If not, the controller will always perform doppler tuning and "
"you cannot use the same RIG for uplink.\n"
"\n"
"<b>TX only:</b>  The radio shall only be used for uplink. If <i>Monitor PTT "
"status</i> is checked the doppler tuning will be suspended while PTT is OFF "
"(manual RX).\n"
"\n"
"<b>Half-duplex:</b>  The radio should be used for both up- and downlink but "
"not at the same time. This option requires that the PTT status is monitored "
"(otherwise gpredict cannot know whether to tune the RX or the TX).\n"
"\n"
"<b>Full-duplex:</b>  The radio is a full-duplex radio, such as the IC910H. "
"Gpredict will be continuously tuning both uplink and downlink simultaneously "
"and not care about PTT setting.\n"
"\n"
"<b>FT817/857/897 (auto):</b> This is a special mode that can be used with "
"YAESU FT-817, 857 and 897 radios. These radios do not allow computer control "
"while in TX mode. Therefore, TX Doppler correction is applied while the "
"radio is in RX mode by toggling between VFO A/B.\n"
"\n"
"<b>FT817/857/897 (manual):</b> This is similar to the previous mode except "
"that switching to TX is done by pressing the SPACE key on the keyboard. "
"Gpredict will then update the TX Doppler before actually switching to TX."
msgstr ""
"<b>Kun RX:</b>  Radioen bruges kun som modtager. Hvis <i>Overvåg PTT-status</i> er markeret, suspenderes dopplerjusteringen, mens PTT er TIL (manuel TX). Hvis ikke, foretager kontrolleren altid dopplerjustering, og du kan ikke bruge den samme RIG til uplink.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Kun TX:</b>  Radioen bruges kun til uplink. Hvis <i>Overvåg PTT-status</i> er markeret, suspenderes dopplerjusteringen, mens PTT er FRA (manuel RX).\n"
"\n"
"<b>Halv-duplex:</b>  Radioen skal bruges til både up- og downlink, men ikke på samme tid. Denne indstilling kræver, at PTT-status overvåges (ellers kan gpredict ikke vide, om RX eller TX skal justeres).\n"
"\n"
"<b>Fuld-duplex:</b>  Radioen er en fuld-duplex-radio, såsom IC910H. Gpredict justerer løbende både uplink og downlink samtidigt og tager ikke hensyn til PTT-indstillingen.\n"
"\n"
"<b>FT817/857/897 (auto):</b> Dette er en særlig tilstand, der kan bruges med YAESU FT-817-, 857- og 897-radioer. Disse radioer tillader ikke computerstyring i TX-tilstand. Derfor anvendes TX-Dopplerkorrektion, mens radioen er i RX-tilstand, ved at skifte mellem VFO A/B.\n"
"\n"
"<b>FT817/857/897 (manuel):</b> Dette ligner den forrige tilstand, bortset fra at skift til TX sker ved at trykke på MELLEMRUM-tasten på tastaturet. Gpredict opdaterer så TX-Doppler, før der faktisk skiftes til TX."

#. ptt
#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:352
msgid "PTT status"
msgstr "PTT-status"

#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:358
msgid "Read PTT"
msgstr "Læs PTT"

#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:359
msgid "Read DCD"
msgstr "Læs DCD"

#: ../src/sat-pref-rig-editor.c:363
msgid ""
"Select PTT type.\n"
"\n"
"<b>None:</b>\n"
"Don't read PTT status from this radio.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Read PTT:</b>\n"
"Read PTT status using get_ptt CAT command. You have to check that your radio "
"and hamlib supports this.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Read DCD:</b>\n"
"Read PTT status using get_dcd command. This can be used if your radio does "
"not support the read_ptt CAT command and you have a special interface that "
"can read squelch status and send it via CTS."
msgstr ""
"Vælg PTT-type.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Ingen:</b>\n"
"Læs ikke PTT-status fra denne radio.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Læs PTT:</b>\n"
"Læs PTT-status med CAT-kommandoen get_ptt. Du skal kontrollere, at din radio og hamlib understøtter dette.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Læs DCD:</b>\n"
"Læs PTT-status med kommandoen get_dcd. Dette kan bruges, hvis din radio ikke understøtter CAT-kommandoen read_ptt, og du har en særlig grænseflade, der kan læse squelch-status og sende den via CTS."

